WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to talk about
your movie.

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:02.469 size:84% position:42% line:92%
But it's very exciting.

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:04.170
You're also working on
the reboot of "Roseanne."

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:04.838 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Roseanne. Roseanne.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:05.672 line:92%
-You're an executive producer.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Didn't we watch "Roseanne"
growing up?

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:07.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, cool.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you -- Here is a photo of
you on set,

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:11.511 size:84% position:42% line:92%
which is very exciting.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.514 size:78% position:39%
-That's on the couch.
-That's on the couch.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.582 size:81% position:41% line:92%
What has it been like?

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:18.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's been a nightmare.
-Uh-huh.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:19.853 line:92%
-You've worked with your heroes.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:22.088
Or you have to talk to
your heroes all the time.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. And at "SNL,"
certainly that was --

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.459
-You're talking to me right now.
This must be hard for you.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:29.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'm just barely,
barely keeping it together.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously,
you're a hero of mine.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's why we gave you
this paper cup.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.633 line:92%
-[ Laughing ] That's right.

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
I get a lot of respect
around here.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:35.602 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:39.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, for me, I was so
excited to work on "Roseanne."

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.941 line:92%
And I just -- I didn't foresee

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
how nervous I'd get around
John Goodman.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:45.178 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:46.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm such a big fan of
John Goodman.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's the sweetest person
on Earth.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:49.549 line:92%
-The nicest, the most talented.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:52.986
And it's weird because growing
up, he was kind of like my dad,

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:55.188
but now, I kind of have a crush
on him.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:56.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's weird.
I have bad thoughts.

00:00:56.623 --> 00:01:00.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I do this thing, I guess,
when I get nervous around

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
a celebrity
that I'm starstruck by.

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:06.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just start lying.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:08.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
I try to just
ignore him entirely

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I know
I'll embarrass myself.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he asked me
how my weekend was,

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:14.407 size:88% position:44%
which should have been
a really quick exchange.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:14.941 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had been on a book tour
at the time.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I was like,
"I was on a book tour."

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.412 line:92%
He's like, "Where did you go?"

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:22.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Oh, I went to
Florida, New York, St. Louis."

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was like,
"Well, I'm from St. Louis."

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:28.188
And in that moment, I realized
I had not been to St. Louis.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:28.888 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:29.789 line:92%
I was going to St. Louis.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:33.026
But I couldn't say,
"Actually, I just lied to you."

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:36.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like that was -- So I just had
to like lean in.

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's like,
"Where did you perform?"

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was, like,
"The Panthenon."

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.134 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.669
Because that kind of sounds like
a theater.

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:44.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure, yes.
-Like the Paramount.

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would believe
there's a Panthenon. Yeah.

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:47.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. And he's like,
"When did that get built?"

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like, "You don't know
about the Panthenon?"

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:53.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I'm, like,
making him feel bad

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:56.382 line:92%
for not knowing about St. Louis.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:59.119 size:78% position:39%
And then, he's like,
"Where did you stay?"

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"The Doubletree."

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:02.188 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's like, "There's
a Doubletree in St. Louis?"

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:08.228
And I'm like, "The one city
there's not a Doubletree

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:08.928 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is the one I lied."

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:11.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now, the window
has closed for this.

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:14.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if he watches this show,
I am fired.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:14.534 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.970
But, so, somewhere, John Goodman
is trying to book a hotel

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
at a Doubletree
that doesn't exist.

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:22.208
-And he can't believe he can't
get a show at the Panthenon.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:22.809 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:23.409 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, totally.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:26.246
And like, I just -- I'm not good
with meeting my heroes.

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:26.980 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I, just, I can't do it.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:30.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
One time, John Cleese -- I did
something with John Cleese.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.718 line:92%
-That's one for me as well. Yup.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:32.652 line:92%
-I don't know. Monty Python.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he came into my dressing
room, and we're talking.

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.623 size:78% position:39%
And I was just, like,
trying to seem cool.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:38.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"I'm just going to, like,

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:39.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
have a drink of whatever
I'm drinking."

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:43.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a lit candle.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:47.867
Literally, it gets to here
and I'm, like, "Oh, my God!"

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:48.668 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:49.769 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You know, so I just --

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:53.940
I don't think I'm designed to be
around my heroes.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.042 size:78% position:39%
-I want to talk about
"The Female Brain."

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:59.679
-By the way, I didn't bring
this out here for that prop.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.381 line:92%
It just worked out that way.

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.248 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Look, you know what?

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am not a prop comic.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.886 size:84% position:42%
I just want you to know
I'm getting a migraine.

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:09.756 size:78% position:39%
So I brought this out
because I need it.

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:10.323 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Just to be clear.

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, well,
we all love the prop bit.

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:13.893 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And now you ruined it.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:14.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sorry.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:17.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Guys, I know you loved
how I have the prop.

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:19.432 line:92%
I have a terrible migraine."

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:20.567 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-And so, my umbrella.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:21.267 size:75% position:38% line:92%
That was fortuitous.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:24.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, this is based on a book
by on the same name,

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:24.871 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"The Female Brain."

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.906
How did you find -- How did you
come across the book?

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:30.143
-Do you ever shop online and the
store you're shopping at, like,

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:33.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
judges you with the purchases
they suggest?

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.951
-My Amazon, the things they
suggest to me are so insulting.

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:40.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I'll be like,
"I need to buy a rubber band."

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:43.823
And it's like, "Did you mean
'Chicken Soup for the Soul?'"

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:45.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "No!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I'm just, like, buying
because I guess

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:49.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do buy a lot of
self-help books.

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:50.129 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Not that I need it.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:50.930 line:92%
And they kept suggesting --

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.700
users who bought this item also
bought "The Female Brain."

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like,
"I should just buy this

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:58.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they're going to keep
harassing me about it."

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:58.805 line:92%
So I finally just bought it.

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:04.410
And then I read it, and it was
so empowering and interesting,

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was like,
"I just really --

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:06.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we should
make a movie of this."

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:09.249
I asked our friend Neil Brennan
if he would write with me.

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:10.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Neil Brennan, another very
funny comedian.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:12.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys have known each other
for years.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:14.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Created "The Chappelle Show"
with Dave Chappelle.

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
No big deal. Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:19.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How was --
How was collaborating?

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:22.629
Obviously, this is a film about
how the brains are different.

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:25.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys have
very different brains.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:25.598 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How was that?

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, when you write with
someone,

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, especially of
the opposite sex,

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.771
it's like all the negative parts
of a relationship

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:32.839 line:92%
and none of the positive parts.

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:35.642
It was only like -- it was just
fighting and driving

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:37.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
and no sex or vacationing.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:40.580
So we basically just tried to
make it as real as possible.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we put ourselves in
situations

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:44.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we could actually
just fight it --

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:46.152 size:75% position:38%
the actual scene out
and transcribe it.

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:49.188
So we basically just, like,
got paid to fight all day.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's not bad.
-It's like my dream job.

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:52.325 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:53.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so we just
knocked it out.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know Neil.
He's the funniest.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:55.728 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Great cast.

00:04:55.728 --> 00:05:00.600
Sofia Vergara, Cecily Strong,
James Marsden, Blake Griffin.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
Blake Griffin is so funny.
It's unfair.

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:05.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Comedy marvel?
-Comedy genius.

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Legend in the making?
-Yeah.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:10.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
Blake Griffin, NBA superstar,
is way too funny.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's actually embarrassing.
-Yeah.

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:15.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-To people whose first job
is to do comedy.

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:19.085
Like, we're all just like,
"Oh, my God. This is bad."

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:22.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is, like, his hobby.
He's better at this.

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:23.523 line:92%
So, he is such a natural.

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:25.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, like, he improvised
a lot of it.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:27.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't even take credit
for a lot of it.

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:31.064
Neil knew him and, you know,
suggested it and made it happen.

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:31.631 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's great.

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:33.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think
you'll be very delighted.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:35.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are going to make
Blake Griffin

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:36.469 line:92%
a different kind of star.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Like, he needed some cash.

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:39.272 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.641 size:78% position:39%
But it's obviously --
He was also so tall.

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:42.175 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank, God.

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:44.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
Cecily, we had to put her in
these huge heels

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
just so they could fit
in the same frame

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:48.448
because Blake is so tall,
it's hard to shoot him.

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:51.851
You just see, like, Blake
and, like clouds, you know?

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:52.418 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:54.687
We had to get all these special
things to shoot him.

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:56.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was pretty funny.
-Well, well done.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:06:00.259
And always so great to see you,
Whitney. Congrats on the movie.

